I had no savings.

00:10:00.808 --> 00:10:05.737
And I had very few networks,
almost nothing in Latin America.

00:10:05.737 --> 00:10:12.777
And I wanted to embark on this journey to
launch a continental social enterprise,

00:10:12.777 --> 00:10:18.620
which is way out of proportion for
what I could do at the time.

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:23.747
So for me, going to the GSB for
a couple of years to give myself time

00:10:23.747 --> 00:10:30.010
to develop the idea, develop myself,
build networks, was really valuable.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:36.150
Also because the program that I wanted
to build was focused on leadership and

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:39.010
from my read of different MBA programs.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:42.534
I almost saw the GSB as more of
a leadership masters than a traditional

00:10:42.534 --> 00:10:46.140
business masters, and it seemed like
it was the best one in the world.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:51.270
So I wanted to see from within what was so
good about it to get inspired.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.496
But, I mean, both to build up myself and
to become inspired for

00:10:53.496 --> 00:10:54.850
what we could build in Latin America.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:11:02.606
So yeah, those are a couple of
the biggest reasons for me.

00:11:02.606 --> 00:11:04.490
